            <email>Elchi3@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/Elchi3</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2025-08-07T10:32:59.000Z</published>
    </entry>
    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Indicate `InputDeviceInfo` is not available in Firefox]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27521</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27521"/>
        <updated>2025-08-08T08:30:03.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6960788?u=0f065d939acde32c4377d427c2d3181b50c65ced&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Marks <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/InputDeviceInfo" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">InputDeviceInfo</code></a> as unsupported by firefox.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">Noticed issue by trying <a href="https://jsfiddle.net/6x3dr7hL/" rel="nofollow">this jsfiddle</a>, which is simply <code class="notranslate">const info = MediaDeviceInfo</code>, and results in <code class="notranslate">InputDeviceInfo is not defined</code> in current Firefox.</p>
<p dir="auto">Tried to find a few citable sources to substantiate the claim, here's what I found on searchfox.org:</p>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-enumerateDevices.https.html.ini" rel="nofollow">MediaDevices-enumerateDevices.https.html.ini</a>:</p>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="[InputDeviceInfo is supported]
  expected: FAIL"><pre class="notranslate"><code class="notranslate">[InputDeviceInfo is supported]
  expected: FAIL
</code></pre></div>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-streams/idlharness.https.window.js.ini" rel="nofollow">idlharness.https.window.js.ini</a>:</p>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="  [InputDeviceInfo interface: existence and properties of interface prototype object]
    expected: FAIL
"><pre class="notranslate"><code class="notranslate">  [InputDeviceInfo interface: existence and properties of interface prototype object]
    expected: FAIL

</code></pre></div>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/dom/webidl/moz.build" rel="nofollow">moz.build</a>:</p>
<p dir="auto">Doesn't include <code class="notranslate">InputDeviceInfo.idl</code>, only  <code class="notranslate">MediaDeviceInfo.idl</code>, which <a href="https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/dom/webidl/MediaDeviceInfo.webidl" rel="nofollow">doesn't contain <code class="notranslate">InputDeviceInfo</code></a></p>

<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #27495.">fixes</span>: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3292618971" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27495" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27495/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27495">#27495</a></li>
</ul>]]></content>
